   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{(-1)^{n+1}(x - 5)^{n}}{n^{2}\\,6^{n}} \\) for \\( |x - 5| < 6 \\). The sum of the first two terms of this series at \\( x = 7 \\) is used to approximate \\( f(7) \\). Find the alternating series error bound for this approximation."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         1,
         243
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "At \\( x = 7 \\), \\( x - 5 = 2 \\), so the terms are \\( (-1)^{n+1} a_n \\) with \\( a_n = \\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})^{n}}{n^{2}} \\). These alternate in sign and decrease in absolute value to 0.",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The approximation uses terms \\( n = 1 \\) to \\( n = 2 \\), so the first omitted term is the one with \\( n = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Its absolute value is \\( a_{3} = \\frac{1}{243} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            243
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "By the alternating series error bound, the error is at most \\( \\frac{1}{243} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            243
         ]
      }
   ],
